    "body": "As a compromise you could use `ghc -- --numeric-version` to get the global ghc version. Stack lets you pin versions so it wouldn't always be accurate but it would be close. Additionally you could read from one of the three configuration files that haskell projects generally use (listed in the original post). I am not sure how expensive reading from a file buffer would be, or if that is even possible within this project. Let me know if any of these solutions sound reasonable.",
