    "body": "I'm not a Haskell dev myself, so I'm not totally clear on the implications on using `ghc -- --numeric-version` versus what we previously had: `stack ghc -- --numeric-version`. \r\n\r\nReading from files would be preferred over running a command. I would imagine that the values in those files wouldn't necessarily reflect the available Haskell runtime though, only the one that would be preferred for that project. That would unfortunately differ from all the other language and runtime modules, which show the runtime version that will be used. ",
