    "body": "@matchai unfortunately haskell has a couple build tools, so cabal (to my knowledge) uses the global compiler version, while stack uses its own pinned version. So if things were to be done absolutely _correctly_ we would do this:\r\n* Stack: read the lts from stack.yaml (under the top level key `resolver`) and maybe have a map from lts to compiler versions (although this is a bad solution because it would need constant maintenance). A bot could be setup to periodically execute a pull request with info from https://www.stackage.org/snapshots (which I think has an api), but this all seems rather complicated. It would probably be better to just show the lts, and the user can infer the compiler version from that, or just look it up.\r\n* Cabal/Nix: use the global compiler version (`ghc -- --numeric-version`). \r\n\r\n@chipbuster Hey, thanks for adding to the discussion. If I understand you correctly 100-150ms is unacceptably slow (if this is the case I don't think there is a way forward). I think the reason that stack might take a while is it has to check the lts (found in the stack.yaml file) against the compiler version associated with that lts? I am not sure about this, but stack is a haskell abstraction on top of the compiler and isn't heavily optimized (as far as I am aware).\r\n\r\n\r\nAlso, just for reference, spaceship_prompt only checks versions for stack projects and uses the stack command:\r\n```shell\r\nspaceship_haskell() {\r\n  [[ $SPACESHIP_HASKELL_SHOW == false ]] && return\r\n\r\n  # If there are stack files in current directory\r\n  [[ -f stack.yaml ]] || return\r\n\r\n  # The command is stack, so do not change this to haskell.\r\n  spaceship::exists stack || return\r\n\r\n  local haskell_version=$(stack ghc -- --numeric-version --no-install-ghc)\r\n\r\n  spaceship::section \\\r\n    \"$SPACESHIP_HASKELL_COLOR\" \\\r\n    \"$SPACESHIP_HASKELL_PREFIX\" \\\r\n    \"${SPACESHIP_HASKELL_SYMBOL}v${haskell_version}\" \\\r\n    \"$SPACESHIP_HASKELL_SUFFIX\"\r\n}\r\n```",
    "author_association": "NONE",
