    "body": "Huh interesting. Mine is a 2015 as well, but I see numbers that are double yours. Perhaps there's a difference when running in an actual Haskell project directory? Or maybe it depends on if you install haskell platform vs. from homebrew?\r\n\r\nFor Stack, just displaying the resolver version is an interesting idea. Is a stack.yaml without a resolver version considered a valid stack file? Would there be some fallback (perhaps hardcoded into the stack binary) that would be used, or would stack just refuse to touch the file until you specify a resolver?",
