    "body": "system global non-project default options: `/etc/stack/config.yaml`\r\nfor user non-project default options: `~/.stack/config.yaml`\r\n\r\nbut I am pretty sure stack will break if an lts isn't defined. Also, I just learned that since stack 2.0 it can either be called `resolver` or `snapshot` but you can only have one. To answer your question though, I think it would be sufficient to fail and not include anything if the resolver / snapshot isn't specified.\r\n\r\nAfter reading through the other discussions I think someone else suggested stack snapshots as well.\r\n\r\nIt would also be nice to use the global compiler version if there is no `stack.yaml` but there is a `*.cabal` (but I know this is a much bigger ask, especially considering the baseline performance of `ghc -- --numeric-version`)",
